    {
      "id": "n1",
      "kind": "grammar",
      "title": "One verb form for everyone",
      "text": "In Norwegian the verb does not change with the person: \"Anna drikker\", \"Lars drikker\", \"jeg drikker\", \"du drikker\". \"Har\" (has, have) is the same for everyone too. \"Ikke\" (not) comes right after the verb: \"Sam har ikke kaffe\". There is no \"a\" or \"the\" before vann and kaffe, just as in English \"I drink water\".",
